Linux Lab 001 — Server Investigation

whoami       -> Current user
hostname     -> Server hostname
hostnamectl  -> Host and OS information
pwd          -> Current directory
id           -> UID, GID and Groups
uname -r     -> Kernel release
uname -m     -> CPU architecture
free -h      -> RAM and Swap information
uptime       -> Uptime and Load Average

Key Lessons:
- Available memory is often more useful than Free memory.
- Low Free RAM does not automatically mean memory pressure.
- Load Average is not CPU utilization percentage.
- Load Average represents 1, 5 and 15 minute averages.
- Inspect first, diagnose second, modify only when needed.